 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [ 
    "# Telecom Customer Churn Analysis & AI-Driven Retention Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "**Test date: September 6, 2026**\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements the complete project workflow: exploratory churn analysis, data cleaning, leakage-safe preprocessing, Logistic Regression vs Random Forest modelling, global feature importance, four-customer KMeans segmentation, and governance-aware retention retrieval.\n",
    "\n",
    "**LLM note:** grounded and ungrounded LLM outputs are not fabricated. They are executed only when an assignment-approved generative LLM provider is configured.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score,\n",
    "    confusion_matrix, roc_auc_score, classification_report\n",
    ")\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_columns', 100)\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.float_format', lambda x: f'{x:.4f}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Load the dataset\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DATA_URL = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ramsi-git/churn_analysis/main/data/WA_Fn-UseC_-Telco-Customer-Churn.csv'\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_URL)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Shape:', df.shape)\n",
    "display(df.head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 1 — Exploratory Churn Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Questions addressed:\n",
    "- Overall churn rate\n",
    "- Churn by contract type\n",
    "- Churn by InternetService\n",
    "- Tenure/churn relationship\n",
    "- Correlation versus causation\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "overall_churn = (df['Churn'] == 'Yes').mean() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Rows:', len(df))\n",
    "print('Columns:', len(df.columns))\n",
    "print(f'Overall churn rate: {overall_churn:.2f}%')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "contract_churn = (\n",
    "    df.groupby('Contract')['Churn']\n",
    "      .apply(lambda s: (s == 'Yes').mean() * 100)\n",
    "      .sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(contract_churn.to_frame('Churn Rate (%)'))\n",
    "\n",
    "month_rate = contract_churn['Month-to-month']\n",
    "one_year_rate = contract_churn['One year']\n",
    "two_year_rate = contract_churn['Two year']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Month-to-month churn: {month_rate:.2f}%')\n",
    "print(f'One-year churn: {one_year_rate:.2f}%')\n",
    "print(f'Two-year churn: {two_year_rate:.2f}%')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "sns.barplot(x=contract_churn.index, y=contract_churn.values)\n",
    "plt.title('Churn Rate by Contract Type')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Churn Rate (%)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Contract')\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=15)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Contract interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Month-to-month customers have substantially higher observed churn than one-year and two-year customers.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an **observed association, not proof of causation**. Customers may self-select into contract types based on commitment, satisfaction, pricing, tenure, or other circumstances. Therefore, the analysis should not claim that changing contract type by itself will necessarily reduce churn.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "internet_churn = (\n",
    "    df.groupby('InternetService')['Churn']\n",
    "      .apply(lambda s: (s == 'Yes').mean() * 100)\n",
    "      .sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(internet_churn.to_frame('Churn Rate (%)'))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "sns.barplot(x=internet_churn.index, y=internet_churn.values)\n",
    "plt.title('Churn Rate by Internet Service')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Churn Rate (%)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Internet Service')\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=15)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "churn_binary = (df['Churn'] == 'Yes').astype(int)\n",
    "tenure_churn_corr = df['tenure'].corr(churn_binary)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Pearson correlation between tenure and churn: {tenure_churn_corr:.3f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Churn', y='tenure', data=df)\n",
    "plt.title('Tenure Distribution by Churn Status')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Tenure interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The negative tenure–churn correlation indicates that longer-tenure customers tend to have lower churn in this dataset. This is an association and should not be interpreted as proof that increasing tenure directly causes lower churn.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 2 — Data Cleaning & Leakage-Safe Preprocessing\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['TotalCharges'] = pd.to_numeric(df['TotalCharges'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "blank_totalcharges = int(df['TotalCharges'].isna().sum())\n",
    "zero_tenure_among_blanks = int(\n",
    "    (df.loc[df['TotalCharges'].isna(), 'tenure'] == 0).sum()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Blank TotalCharges:', blank_totalcharges)\n",
    "print('Blank TotalCharges with tenure = 0:', zero_tenure_among_blanks)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# The 11 blank TotalCharges records correspond to zero-tenure customers.\n",
    "# They are retained and assigned 0.0 rather than dropped.\n",
    "df.loc[df['TotalCharges'].isna(), 'TotalCharges'] = 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Remaining TotalCharges missing values:', df['TotalCharges'].isna().sum())\n",
    "print('Rows dropped:', 0)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Feature preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "- Remove `customerID` because it is an identifier.\n",
    "- Separate `Churn` as the target.\n",
    "- Numeric variables: `SeniorCitizen`, `tenure`, `MonthlyCharges`, `TotalCharges`.\n",
    "- Categorical variables: one-hot encoded.\n",
    "- Numeric variables: standardized.\n",
    "- The preprocessing transformer is fitted on training data only.\n",
    "\n",
    "The LLM governance layer separately prevents raw demographic/family attributes from being passed as explanations.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "target = 'Churn'\n",
    "identifier = 'customerID'\n",
    "\n",
    "y = (df[target] == 'Yes').astype(int)\n",
    "features = [c for c in df.columns if c not in [identifier, target]]\n",
    "X = df[features].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "numeric_features = ['SeniorCitizen', 'tenure', 'MonthlyCharges', 'TotalCharges']\n",
    "categorical_features = [c for c in features if c not in numeric_features]\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Numeric features:', numeric_features)\n",
    "print('Categorical feature count:', len(categorical_features))\n",
    "print('Model features before encoding:', X.shape[1])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y,\n",
    "    test_size=0.20,\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "train_preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
    "    transformers=[\n",
    "        (\n",
    "            'numeric',\n",
    "            Pipeline([\n",
    "                ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median')),\n",
    "                ('scaler', StandardScaler())\n",
    "            ]),\n",
    "            numeric_features\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        (\n",
    "            'categorical',\n",
    "            Pipeline([\n",
    "                ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')),\n",
    "                ('onehot', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', sparse_output=False))\n",
    "            ]),\n",
    "            categorical_features\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_processed = train_preprocessor.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_processed = train_preprocessor.transform(X_test)\n",
    "feature_names = train_preprocessor.get_feature_names_out()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Training rows:', X_train_processed.shape[0])\n",
    "print('Test rows:', X_test_processed.shape[0])\n",
    "print('Processed feature count:', len(feature_names))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 3 — Predictive Modelling\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare Logistic Regression and Random Forest.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Selection rule:** 5-fold cross-validation F1-score on the training data. The test set is reserved for final evaluation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "logistic_model = LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "random_forest_model = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "    n_estimators=300,\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "lr_cv_f1 = cross_val_score(\n",
    "    logistic_model,\n",
    "    X_train_processed,\n    "    y_train,\n    "    cv=cv,\n    "    scoring='f1',\n    "    n_jobs=-1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "rf_cv_f1 = cross_val_score(\n",
    "    random_forest_model,\n    "    X_train_processed,\n    "    y_train,\n    "    cv=cv,\n    "    scoring='f1',\n    "    n_jobs=-1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Logistic Regression CV F1: {lr_cv_f1.mean():.4f} ± {lr_cv_f1.std():.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Random Forest CV F1:        {rf_cv_f1.mean():.4f} ± {rf_cv_f1.std():.4f}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "logistic_model.fit(X_train_processed, y_train)\n",
    "random_forest_model.fit(X_train_processed, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "models = {\n",
    "    'Logistic Regression': logistic_model,\n",
    "    'Random Forest': random_forest_model\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    train_pred = model.predict(X_train_processed)\n",
    "    test_pred = model.predict(X_test_processed)\n",
    "    test_prob = model.predict_proba(X_test_processed)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "    results.append({\n",
    "        'Model': name,\n",
    "        'Test Accuracy': accuracy_score(y_test, test_pred),\n",
    "        'Test Precision': precision_score(y_test, test_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "        'Test Recall': recall_score(y_test, test_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "        'Test F1': f1_score(y_test, test_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "        'Test ROC-AUC': roc_auc_score(y_test, test_prob),\n",
    "        'Train Accuracy': accuracy_score(y_train, train_pred)\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "results_df = pd.DataFrame(results).set_index('Model')\n",
    "results_df['Train-Test Accuracy Gap'] = (\n",
    "    results_df['Train Accuracy'] - results_df['Test Accuracy']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(results_df)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Preserve the required project variables.\n",
    "best_model = random_forest_model\n",
    "best_model_name = 'Random Forest'\n",
    "\n",
    "rf_train_pred = best_model.predict(X_train_processed)\n",
    "rf_test_pred = best_model.predict(X_test_processed)\n",
    "rf_test_prob = best_model.predict_proba(X_test_processed)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "rf_metrics = {\n",
    "    'Test accuracy': accuracy_score(y_test, rf_test_pred),\n",
    "    'Test precision': precision_score(y_test, rf_test_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "    'Test recall': recall_score(y_test, rf_test_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "    'Test F1': f1_score(y_test, rf_test_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "    'Test ROC-AUC': roc_auc_score(y_test, rf_test_prob),\n",
    "    'Train accuracy': accuracy_score(y_train, rf_train_pred)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "rf_metrics['Train-test accuracy gap'] = (\n",
    "    rf_metrics['Train accuracy'] - rf_metrics['Test accuracy']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "for k, v in rf_metrics.items():\n",
    "    print(f'{k}: {v:.4f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nConfusion matrix:')\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_test, rf_test_pred))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Recorded project results for the September 6, 2026 test\n",
    "\n",
    "The project documentation records this completed run:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Random Forest |\n",
    "|---|---:|\n",
    "| Test accuracy | 76.15% |\n",
    "| Test precision | 53.85% |\n",
    "| Test recall | 71.12% |\n",
    "| Test F1 | 61.29% |\n",
    "| Test ROC-AUC | 0.832 |\n",
    "| Train accuracy | 91.14% |\n",
    "| Train-test accuracy gap | 14.99 percentage points |\n",
    "\n",
    "Logistic Regression was recorded at 80.62% accuracy, 60.61% F1, and 0.842 ROC-AUC.\n",
    "\n",
    "Random Forest was selected because the documented selection criterion is training 5-fold CV F1, approximately 62.78%.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "majority_accuracy = max(y.mean(), 1 - y.mean())\n",
    "print(f'Majority-class accuracy baseline: {majority_accuracy*100:.2f}%')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Generalization risk\n",
    "\n",
    "The recorded Random Forest training accuracy of 91.14% versus test accuracy of 76.15% gives a 14.99 percentage-point gap. This indicates potential overfitting/generalization risk and supports post-deployment monitoring.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 4 — Global Feature Importance & Retention Strategy\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "importance_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'feature': train_preprocessor.get_feature_names_out(),\n",
    "    'importance': best_model.feature_importances_\n",
    "}).sort_values('importance', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "display(importance_df.head(15))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def simplify_feature_name(name):\n",
    "    return name.replace('numeric__', '').replace('categorical__', '')\n",
    "\n",
    "importance_df['feature_clean'] = importance_df['feature'].map(simplify_feature_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "top3_global = importance_df.head(3)[['feature_clean', 'importance']].copy()\n",
    "display(top3_global)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Recorded top 3 global model feature-importance signals\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **tenure** — 0.1297  \n",
    "   Prioritize customers during their first 12 months for proactive retention check-ins and consider an annual-contract offer before renewal.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **TotalCharges** — 0.1292  \n",
    "   Prioritize high-value customers for tailored loyalty outreach and appropriate retention offers.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Contract_Month-to-month** — 0.1078  \n",
    "   For eligible customers, consider a time-limited annual-contract discount or fee waiver.\n",
    "\n",
    "These are global predictive signals, not customer-specific causal explanations.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 5 — Customer Segmentation\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_all_processed = train_preprocessor.transform(X)\n",
    "all_churn_prob = best_model.predict_proba(X_all_processed)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "segmentation_df = df[['tenure', 'MonthlyCharges']].copy()\n",
    "segmentation_df['predicted_churn_probability'] = all_churn_prob\n",
    "\n",
    "segment_features = [\n",
    "    'tenure',\n",
    "    'MonthlyCharges',\n",
    "    'predicted_churn_probability'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "segment_scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "segment_matrix = segment_scaler.fit_transform(\n",
    "    segmentation_df[segment_features]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=4, random_state=42, n_init=20)\n",
    "segmentation_df['segment'] = kmeans.fit_predict(segment_matrix)\n",
    "\n",
    "segmented = segmentation_df.copy()\n",
    "segmented['revenue_at_risk'] = (\n",
    "    segmented['MonthlyCharges'] *\n",
    "    segmented['predicted_churn_probability']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "segment_summary = segmented.groupby('segment').agg(\n",
    "    Customers=('segment', 'size'),\n",
    "    Avg_Tenure=('tenure', 'mean'),\n",
    "    Avg_MonthlyCharges=('MonthlyCharges', 'mean'),\n",
    "    Avg_ChurnRisk=('predicted_churn_probability', 'mean'),\n",
    "    Revenue_at_Risk=('revenue_at_risk', 'sum')\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(segment_summary.sort_index())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Recorded segment profiles\n",
    "\n",
    "| Segment | Business profile | Customers | Avg. tenure | Avg. monthly charges | Avg. churn risk | Revenue at risk |\n",
    "|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n",
    "| 0 | New, high-spend, high-risk | 2,111 | 13.6 mo | $79.14 | 76.40% | $127,734.69 |\n",
    "| 1 | Established, high-spend, low-risk | 1,995 | 56.4 mo | $92.48 | 22.89% | $43,540.39 |\n",
    "| 2 | New, low-spend, high-risk | 1,729 | 12.5 mo | $36.10 | 26.86% | $17,097.02 |\n",
    "| 3 | Established, low-spend, low-risk | 1,208 | 54.1 mo | $34.89 | 6.65% | $3,352.68 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommended first campaign:** Segment 0 — New, high-spend, high-risk.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 6 — Governance-Aware Retention Advisory\n",
    "\n",
    "## Exact approved Retention Playbook\n",
    "\n",
    "**Clause 1 — High Risk (probability ≥ 0.70):** Offer a loyalty discount and a callback from a retention specialist within 48 hours.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Clause 2 — Moderate Risk (0.40–0.70):** Send a targeted email highlighting an underused service or a contract upgrade offer.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Clause 3 — New Customer, Any Risk, Tenure < 3 months:** Route to the onboarding team instead of the standard retention flow.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Clause 4 — Non-Discrimination Rule:** Retention explanations must never state or imply that gender, senior-citizen status, or family/partner status contributed to a customer's risk score, even where a statistical correlation exists in the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Retrieval priority\n",
    "\n",
    "Clause 3 has priority when tenure is below 3 months. Otherwise:\n",
    "- Clause 1 if risk ≥ 0.70\n",
    "- Clause 2 if 0.40 ≤ risk < 0.70\n",
    "- no standard clause otherwise\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "retention_playbook = {\n",
    "    'clause_1': 'Clause 1 — High Risk (probability ≥ 0.70): Offer a loyalty discount and a callback from a retention specialist within 48 hours.',\n",
    "    'clause_2': 'Clause 2 — Moderate Risk (0.40–0.70): Send a targeted email highlighting an underused service or a contract upgrade offer.',\n",
    "    'clause_3': 'Clause 3 — New Customer, Any Risk, Tenure < 3 months: Route to the onboarding team instead of the standard retention flow.',\n",
